    "body": "Escalated to `effort:max` before a claim. Codex (skull) did no code work. No branch was made.\n\nWhat I found on upstream/main `dfbe0d8a5`:\n\n- `camcraft_post::machine::kind::Kind` has no `Router` variant. A router file is a `Mill` now.\n- A new variant changes the exhaustive matches on `Kind` in about 33 source files in 5 crates: `post`, `app`, `tools`, `ui` and the MCP code. Examples are `crates/app/src/operation/kinds.rs`, `crates/app/src/posting_serves.rs`, `crates/tools/src/tool_sanity.rs` and `crates/ui/src/machine_modes.rs`. Each match needs a decision: does a router act as a mill there?\n- The \"one function decides what a kind shows\" law does not exist yet for operations and pages. `crates/ui/src/machine_modes.rs` has `tool_kind_offered_for` for tools only. The new function must be in `app`, because MCP must read it too.\n- Most of the content to show is not built:\n  - The Nest node is #2163 (open).\n  - The router machine files are #1915 and #1918 (open).\n  - Of the router option issues, only #2400 and #2407 are closed. #2398, #2399, #2401, #2402, #2404, #2405, #2406, #2408 and #2409 are open.\n\nRecommendation: split this issue in two.\n\n1. Add `Kind::Router` (declared only, like plasma) and the visibility function in `app`, with a UI test and an MCP test. The function shows the corner relief of #2400 and the tool-change macros of #2407 for a router, and hides them for a mill.\n2. Each open router issue adds its row to that function when it ships.\n\nThe work is larger than `effort:high` (open design, five crates, a new law that UI and MCP share). I raised the label one step.\n",
